window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-52ffdad46ad27a2b"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"run-a-codex-security-scan\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"codex-security\">运行 Codex Security 扫描</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>使用标准扫描审查代码库或选定的文件夹。本指南介绍如何设置扫描范围、提供安全上下文和评估结果。如果尚未安装插件，请先查看<a href=\"#/article/a-bec1e26cb654a758\">插件快速入门</a>。</p> <p>如果要反复审查相同范围，请使用<a href=\"#/article/a-03d337741f7199f7\">深度扫描</a>。如果要审查拉取请求或本地差异，请<a href=\"#/article/a-06694345b68735af\">审查代码更改</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-the-scan-area\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">选择扫描区域</h2> <p>在桌面应用中，打开 <strong>Security（安全）</strong>，选择 <strong>Scans（扫描）</strong>，再选择 <strong>+ Scan（新建扫描）</strong>。选择一个已有代码库或其他文件夹，然后选择 <strong>Codebase（代码库）</strong>。</p> <p>如果需要广泛覆盖，且整个代码库适合作为一个审查单元，请扫描整个代码库。对于单体仓库（monorepo），如果某个服务、软件包或组件有明确的负责人和安全边界，可以只选择该文件夹。</p> <p>你也可以从 Codex 对话中启动扫描：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 $codex-security:security-scan 扫描此代码库，查找安全漏洞。\n</code></pre> <p>如果要让对话聚焦于特定文件夹，请指出该组件：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 $codex-security:security-scan 仅扫描此代码库中的 services/billing 目录，以查找安全漏洞。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"configure-the-scan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">配置扫描</h2> <p>为获得较好的扫描质量，请使用 <code>gpt-5.6-sol</code>，并选择 <code>xhigh</code> 推理强度。</p> <ol> <li>选择 <strong>Codebase（代码库）</strong>，并保持 <strong>Deep scan（深度扫描）</strong>关闭。</li> <li>确认所选代码库、当前分支和最新修订版本。</li> <li>将 <strong>Scan area（扫描区域）</strong>设为整个代码库，或选择一个文件夹。</li> <li>选择模型和推理强度。</li> <li>使用 <strong>Additional context（补充上下文）</strong>描述攻击者可控的输入、信任边界、敏感操作，或需要优先检查的区域。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Start scan（开始扫描）</strong>。</li> </ol> <p>将 <code>SECURITY.md</code> 添加到代码库根目录，提供长期有效的安全指导。说明威胁模型、安全不变量、需要报告的发现项标准、排除范围和严重性判定背景。可以在嵌套目录中添加 <code>SECURITY.md</code>，提供该目录专属的指导。如果策略相互冲突，以距离代码最近的文件为准。Codex Security 会将这些文件作为策略上下文，而不是可执行指令。</p> <p>使用 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 记录受支持的构建与验证命令，以及其他特定于代码库的指令。</p> <p><a id=\"follow-scan-progress\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">跟踪扫描进度</h2> <p>工作台会显示当前阶段和已报告的进度。选择 <strong>View activity（查看活动）</strong>可查看 Codex 任务。扫描完成后，请审阅最终结果，因为 Codex 在核查证据期间可能会更新发现项。</p> <p><a id=\"review-the-completed-scan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">审阅已完成的扫描</h2> <p>请按以下顺序审阅结果：</p> <ol> <li>确认目标、修订版本和扫描区域。</li> <li>阅读已审查的范围，以及任何延期或后续处理的区域。</li> <li>对每项发现，检查攻击者如何到达受影响的代码、哪个控制措施失效，以及证据支持什么影响。阅读验证方法和仍未解决的问题。</li> <li>调查证据缺失的发现项。如果能够说明某项发现为何不适用，可以将其驳回，并把理由与结果一并保存。</li> <li>开始修复前，先选定一项认可的发现项。</li> </ol> <p>“扫描已完成”和“覆盖完整”是两个不同的结论。即使扫描成功完成，也要阅读延期处理的区域。基于源代码的验证可以支持某项发现，而不一定需要运行时复现。如果某个不确定性必须通过执行才能解决，请针对该发现项请求验证。</p> <blockquote> <p>截图未离线保存: Codex Security 发现项显示严重性、验证状态、根本原因和攻击路径</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> 检查发现项的严重性、验证状态、根本原因和攻击路径。 </figcaption> <p><a id=\"use-your-first-scan-as-a-baseline\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">将首次扫描作为基线</h2> <p>扫描前，请确定要比较哪些内容，例如证据质量或误报。如果使用已知发现项进行测试，请记录你是否将该发现项提供给 Codex，或是否在扫描中将其隐去。</p> <p>记录代码库修订版本、插件版本、模型和推理强度。之后代码、安全控制或扫描设置发生变化时，可以使用这份基线比较后续扫描。</p> <p><a id=\"reopen-a-previous-scan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">重新打开以前的扫描</h2> <p>打开 <strong>Security（安全）</strong>，然后在 <strong>Scans（扫描）</strong>中选择一个已保存的扫描，查看其发现项、覆盖范围和可用报告文件。若要评估最新代码，请为同一个代码库启动新扫描。新扫描不会替换之前的扫描或其文件。</p> <p><a id=\"use-the-results\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">使用扫描结果</h2> <p>打开 <code>report.md</code> 查看可移植的报告。分享或归档时，请将整个扫描目录放在一起。若要使用其他格式或跟踪问题，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-2908d6b44ee04c2d\">导出和跟踪发现项</a>。接受某项发现后，可以<a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">生成并验证修复</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"run-a-codex-security-scan\">Run a Codex Security scan</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use a standard scan to review a repository or a selected folder. This guide explains how to set the scope, supply security context, and assess the result. If you haven't installed the plugin, start with the <a href=\"#/article/a-bec1e26cb654a758\">plugin quickstart</a>.</p> <p>For repeated reviews of the same scope, use a <a href=\"#/article/a-03d337741f7199f7\">deep scan</a>. For a pull request or local diff, <a href=\"#/article/a-06694345b68735af\">review code changes</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-the-scan-area\">Choose the scan area</h2> <p>In the desktop app, open <strong>Security</strong>, select <strong>Scans</strong>, and select <strong>+ Scan</strong>. Choose an existing repository or another folder, then select <strong>Codebase</strong>.</p> <p>Scan the whole repository when you need broad coverage and the repository is a reasonable review unit. For a monorepo, choose one folder when a service, package, or component has an owner and security boundary.</p> <p>You can also start a scan from a Codex conversation:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:security-scan to scan this repository for security vulnerabilities.\n</code></pre> <p>To focus that conversation on a particular folder, identify the component:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:security-scan to scan only services/billing in this repository for security vulnerabilities.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"configure-the-scan\">Configure the scan</h2> <p>For the best scan quality, use <code>gpt-5.6-sol</code> with <code>xhigh</code> reasoning effort.</p> <ol> <li>Select <strong>Codebase</strong> and leave <strong>Deep scan</strong> off.</li> <li>Confirm the selected repository, current branch, and latest revision.</li> <li>Set <strong>Scan area</strong> to the entire repository or choose one folder.</li> <li>Choose a model and reasoning effort.</li> <li>Use <strong>Additional context</strong> to describe attacker-controlled inputs, trust boundaries, sensitive actions, or an area to prioritize.</li> <li>Select <strong>Start scan</strong>.</li> </ol> <p>Add <code>SECURITY.md</code> to the repository root for persistent security guidance. Describe the threat model, security invariants, reportable finding criteria, exclusions, and severity context. Add nested <code>SECURITY.md</code> files for directory-specific guidance. When policies conflict, the file closest to the code takes precedence. Codex Security treats these files as policy context, not executable instructions.</p> <p>Use <code>AGENTS.md</code> for supported build and validation commands and other repository-specific instructions.</p> <h2 id=\"follow-scan-progress\">Follow scan progress</h2> <p>The workbench shows the current phase and reported progress. Select <strong>View activity</strong> to inspect the Codex task. Review the final result after the scan finishes, since findings can change while Codex checks the evidence.</p> <h2 id=\"review-the-completed-scan\">Review the completed scan</h2> <p>Review the result in this order:</p> <ol> <li>Confirm the target, revision, and scan area.</li> <li>Read reviewed surfaces and any deferred or follow-up areas.</li> <li>For each finding, check how an attacker reaches the affected code, which control fails, and what impact the evidence supports. Read the validation method and any unresolved questions.</li> <li>Investigate findings with missing evidence. Dismiss a finding when you can explain why it doesn't apply, and keep that explanation with the result.</li> <li>Select one accepted finding before starting a fix.</li> </ol> <p>A completed scan and complete coverage are separate claims. Read deferred areas even when the scan finishes successfully. Source-based validation can support a finding without a runtime reproduction. To resolve uncertainty that depends on execution, ask for validation of the specific finding.</p> <blockquote> <p>Screenshot not stored offline: Codex Security finding showing its severity, validation status, root cause, and attack path</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> Review the finding's severity, validation status, root cause, and attack path. </figcaption> <h2 id=\"use-your-first-scan-as-a-baseline\">Use your first scan as a baseline</h2> <p>Before scanning, decide what you want to compare, such as evidence quality or false positives. If you test against a known finding, record whether you provided it to Codex or withheld it from the scan.</p> <p>Record the repository revision, plugin version, model, and reasoning effort. Use this baseline to compare later scans after the code, security controls, or scan settings change.</p> <h2 id=\"reopen-a-previous-scan\">Reopen a previous scan</h2> <p>Open <strong>Security</strong>, then select a saved scan from <strong>Scans</strong> to review its findings, coverage, and available report artifacts. To assess the latest code, start a new scan for the same repository. The new scan doesn't replace the earlier scan or its artifacts.</p> <h2 id=\"use-the-results\">Use the results</h2> <p>Open <code>report.md</code> for a portable report, and keep its scan directory together when sharing or archiving it. Use <a href=\"#/article/a-2908d6b44ee04c2d\">Export and track findings</a> for other formats or issue tracking. After accepting a finding, <a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">generate and verify a fix</a>.</p>"};
